<title>FRANCE: New York top originating gateway in April 97.</title>
<headline>New York top originating gateway in April 97.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in April 1997.</p>
<p>The top ten  destinations  for ADP exports in  April 1997 and, the percentage change on April 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>    Origin			Percent</p>
<p>			  tonnes Change 1996</p>
<p> 1. New York	   2776   down  9.2</p>
<p> 2. Chicago	    2372     up  7.2</p>
<p> 3. Hong Kong	  2131     up 18.5</p>
<p> 4. Tokyo		2130   down  3.1</p>
<p> 5. Montreal	   1122     up  5.1</p>
<p> 6. Mexico City	1108     up 44.3</p>
<p> 7. Singapore	   791     up 22.8</p>
<p> 8. Sao Paulo	   764   down 25.7</p>
<p> 9. Dubai		 714   down 21.8</p>
<p> 10 Miami		 697     up  6.8</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
<p>www.racs.com</p>
